//! The `border-width` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property sets the width of an element's border.
//!
//! Initial: border-top-width: medium; border-right-width: medium; border-bottom-width: medium;
//! border-left-width: medium. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - medium: Same as `3px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border-top-width
//! - thick: Same as `5px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border-top-width
//! - thin: Same as `1px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border-top-width
//!
//! Grammar: <'border-top-width'>{1,4}
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border-width
